      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Select the function that is continuous at $x=-1.$",
      "worked_solution": "Of the given options, the only one where we can draw the graph of the function without taking our pencil off of the paper in a neighborhood of $x=-1$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14227671/assets/ca4279200e98b57570030ea6ecce9c04412645ff16d532f302cb13c6bf59c15e.png)\n\nAll other given options have breaks or asymptotes at $x=-1$, so it is impossible to draw the function in the neighborhood of $x=-1$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.",
